  Its a well made movie, but its no Spirited Away.
---

> See with eyes unclouded by hate.

Great story that touches on human psyche, the ambiguity of good v evil, the cycle of hatred and the importance of coexistence. Ashitaka is a well written character who can strike the balance between this warrior shaped by industrialization and revolution and one being in tune with nature. His scar is not just a literal symbol of the price of hatred but also the balance between nature and civilization. I liked San's development as she struggles with her own identity and also the contrast with Lady Eboshi, who is firm in herself but whose ideals end up being her own downfall.

Its a well made movie, but its no Spirited Away.
